+You are fix lane **fix-density** for melon-seek (/home/user/melon-seek, "the Zillow of job postings"). Save this prompt verbatim to docs/process/prompts/fix-density.md, and write your log to docs/process/fix-density.md following docs/process/TEMPLATE.md. Follow docs/strategy/ROADMAP.md §8 (the UI simplicity budget) and docs/process/prompts/cycle/fix-lane.md.
+
+The user, 2026-10-11: "That footer and top notes esp on the mobile. Eg '564 postings with salary · row medians: pay in the US (55 paid elsewhere left out) · 46 on-target earnings, not in the medians · 81 with no salary posted · yearly pay · 55 converted from another currency at Jul 2026 exchange rates' that's way too busy and too much on a mobile. Make sure you UI/UX QC really do the job and not just gloss experiences like this over. Fix it!"
+
+**Base.** In your worktree run `git checkout --detach 31ad25b`. Symlink node_modules, data/snapshots and data/beta/snapshots from /home/user/melon-seek (today's crawl, all 7 big-tech boards). Commit at milestones, never push, and report your SHAs.
+
+**Do:**
+1. **Inventory every line of secondary text the app shows around the main views.** That means:
+   - the chart's notes line (public/viz/chart.js; the quote above is it) and its caption;
+   - the stats line above the list (public/app.js);
+   - the map's notes and legend text (public/viz/map.js);
+   - the results header and the Insights and Compstimate captions;
+   - the drawer's pay block sub-lines;
+   - empty states and the badge's short label.
+   For each one: board (Amazon, Apple, Google, NVIDIA, Microsoft, Meta, Netflix, Anduril), viewport (390x844 and 360x740 phones, 1440x900 desktop), its full text, its word count, and how many lines it wraps to. Take a screenshot of the worst ones before you change anything.
+2. **Set a rule and apply it everywhere.** Each such line shows at most one short line on a phone and one line on desktop. Keep only the one or two facts a job seeker needs at a glance, for example "564 with pay · 81 without". Everything else goes behind one small, plainly labelled disclosure, for example a "How these numbers work" or "Details" text button that opens a short list, or into the methodology page the app already links. Keep every caveat available, since the reviewers asked for honesty (exchange-rate date, left-out counts, on-target earnings), but not all on the first line. Don't add new controls beyond that one disclosure pattern, and reuse it everywhere. Plain words, no jargon ("row medians" isn't plain).
+3. **Tests that fail today and pass after**, in a NEW file test/e2e/fix-density.e2e.js registered in scripts/e2e.js. On every board, at 390x844 and 360x740, each listed line fits in one line box (or a fixed small height), and stays under a word budget (e.g. 12 words visible). The details are still reachable with a click, and keyboard accessible with aria-expanded. At 1440 there's one line. Update any existing test that pins the old long text, keeping its intent (the fact still exists, under details).
+4. **Before and after screenshots** of every changed line, phone and desktop, light and dark, in docs/screenshots/fix-density/. Shrink them with scripts/cycle/shrink-screenshots.sh.
+
+**You own:** the notes, caption and legend text code in public/viz/chart.js, public/viz/map.js and public/viz/viz.css; the stats line, results header, drawer sub-lines and empty states in public/app.js; public/styles.css for these; and the caption text in public/features/insights.js and compstimate.js. A performance agent runs at the same time and owns public/api.js, public/unpack-worker.js, scripts/build-static.js and scripts/snapshot.js: don't touch those. It may send patches for app.js; keep your changes local to the text you own, so they merge.
+**Gate:** your new tests pass; `npm test` passes with MELON_BETA_SNAPSHOT_DIR set to an empty folder and no data links; the full e2e has no new failures (build with `node scripts/build-static.js --out <scratch>/dist`; tests read BETA_QA_DIST). Check `df -h /`; delete your scratch build when done. Use pid files; never `pkill -f`; never `playwright install` (NODE_PATH=/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-melon-seek/b6b764de-866b-5af7-92f3-f582ebca24d9/scratchpad/pw/node_modules; Chromium /opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194/chrome-linux/chrome). Report the inventory table (before and after word and line counts), the rule you applied, the tests, and your SHAs.
